    "content": {
     "content_type": "text",
     "parts": [
      "Draft:\n\n> Hi [Name],\n>\n> Thanks for reaching out about the P4 late penalty. I double-checked the timestamps. Canvas shows your submission 25 hours 12 minutes after the deadline. Under the syllabus, each started 24-hour period counts as one late day, so P4 used 2 late days. Together with the 2 used on P2, that's 4 of the 3 free late days, which leaves one day at the 10% penalty.\n>\n> I checked this with Dr. [Instructor], and the penalty stands. I understand the 72-minute difference feels small. The policy has to apply the same way to everyone, so I can't make an exception here.\n>\n> If you think the Canvas timestamp is wrong (e.g., an upload error), send me a screenshot or the confirmation email and I'll look again.\n>\n> Best,\n> David\n\nBefore sending, check that the syllabus actually says \"each started 24-hour period\". If it just says \"late day = 24 hours,\" your reading is still the standard one, but quote the exact wording instead of my paraphrase."
     ]
    },
